{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361393,"nonce":"VE4uQGtXQ7DpK4zVl6jjNBZlvpo=","title":"Fibers are freed only when made in a function's entry block and never stored","message":"`LoweringContext::emit_fiber_drops` (crates/compiler/src/lowering.rs) inserts `FiberDrop` before every `Return` for each `FiberNew` result in the function's entry block that is not a `Return` operand and does not flow into a phi; `apply_krio_fiber_lowering` turns it into `__zyntax_effect_fiber_forget` plus `krio_fiber_free`. Every other fiber leaks its box and its mmap'd stack: one created inside a loop or a branch, one received from a call. The escape test ignores stores and call arguments, so an entry-block fiber written into a struct field, or handed to a function that keeps it, is still freed at return while the stored copy lives on (found by reading).\n\nWhat exists: `FiberDrop`, `krio_fiber_free` and `KrioFiberBackend::fiber_free`; the per-task registry that frees a cancelled task's fibers (`krio_adapter::fiber::TASK_FIBERS`); the scope exit-edge walk in `lower_with_scopes`; the ownership model in crates/compiler/src/borrow_check.rs and drop insertion in crates/compiler/src/drop_insert.rs.\n\nDone: a fiber is dropped on every exit edge of the scope that owns it (return, break, continue, fallthrough), and a move (return, store, a call that takes ownership) hands the obligation on instead of freeing. The walk that places the drops is the one `with` pops use (see the with-scope exit edge issue). Tests cover a fiber made in a loop, one returned from a helper, and one stored in a struct.","files":null}]}